  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Willing helpers and small carts can assist from collection to the nearby pickup area; visitors may request help without explaining why they need it.\", \"decision\": \"How should visitors arrange help carrying goods out?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVisitors request carrying help at collection, and a volunteer assigns the next available helper and cart. Assistance follows goods that are ready to leave, keeping the handover simple at the point where carrying begins.\nVisitors reserve a short carrying-help slot when they claim an item and bring their collection record at that time. A planned slot coordinates the recipient and helper before the goods need to move toward the pickup area.\nA helper makes regular rounds between collection and the pickup area, inviting waiting recipients to join the next assisted trip. Several nearby handovers can share one cart journey while visitors retain a visible next opportunity for help."
    }
  ],
